  provenance: "Built from Assets/General Quarters/Prefabs/Models/DDG51_GQ_Layout.json
    (ArtSource/General Quarters/DDG51_GQ.blend via author_ddg51_gq.py).\nMEASURED
    from the hull shell on a 61 x 0.5 m column grid (15976 columns, converged): displacement
    8717 t at the drawn waterline, draft 6.52 m, KB 3.92 m, BM 4.79 m, waterline
    141 \xD7 17.7 m.\nBuoyancy: 2183 columns on a 25 x 1.5 m grid (AUTHORED resolution);
    on their own they displace 8744 t with BM 4.85 m.\nGM 1.50 m: AUTHORED: ~11 s
    natural roll by the IMO formula; DDG-51 KG/GM is not public.\nGyradii: fractions
    of waterline beam/length {\"roll_of_beam\": 0.37, \"pitch_of_length\": 0.25,
    \"yaw_of_length\": 0.25}; roll and yaw from the SIMMAN 2008 DTMB 5415 table (ixx/B
    0.37, izz/Lpp 0.25), pitch AUTHORED.\nCompartments: AUTHORED bulkhead stations
    every 12 m; the real DDG-51 bulkhead plan is not public.\nBuoyancy damping: heave
    ratio 0.2, Cd 0.5 (AUTHORED, Sea State defaults), heave axis only.\nSUBDIVISION
    (Damage Control L1, G53 G54): Blender's 12 stations, each split at the damage-control
    deck into a hold and an upper space; the six midship holds (04-09) also give
    their outboard columns to port and starboard wing spaces. Spaces are cut from
    the buoyancy columns, so their volumes follow the hull. Damage-control deck at
    y +3.4 m (AUTHORED: DDG-51's is the second deck, height not public; about 3 m
    under the main deck amidships). Wing bulkheads at |x| 5.32 m, B/5 in from the
    waterline side (AUTHORED as a position; B/5 is SOLAS's assumed transverse damage
    penetration). Hold uses AUTHORED: 01-03 stores, 04-09 machinery (main and auxiliary
    machinery rooms), 10-11 stores, 12 machinery (steering gear); upper spaces accommodation;
    wing spaces voids. Permeability by use from SOLAS II-1 Reg. 7-3 (public): stores
    0.60, machinery 0.85, accommodation 0.95, void 0.95.\nOPENINGS (G56, all AUTHORED):
    at General Quarters (condition ZEBRA) hatches and doors are shut, so each is
    a leak path: 0.1 m\xB2 per hold hatch through the damage-control deck, 0.1 m\xB2
    per door between neighbouring upper spaces with a 0.3 m sill; 0.5 m\xB2 of weather
    openings (vents, doors, uptakes) per upper space per side at the main deck edge."
